        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: நடைமேடை",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "நடைமேடை — naṭaimēṭai — \"a platform; a raised walkway\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ரயில் மூன்றாவது நடைமேடைக்கு வருகிறது. rayil mūṉṟāvatu naṭaimēṭaikku varukiṟatu. The train is coming to the third platform."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before -க்கு the final -ஐ stays as it is: நடைமேடைக்கு, to the platform."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "நடைமேடை (naṭaimēṭai) is built from naṭai, \"walking, gait\" (DEDR 3582, the family of நட, to walk), and mēṭai, \"a raised floor, a stage\", whose origin is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
