          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ஒத்திவை — ottivai — \"to postpone; to put off\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "மழை பெய்ததால் நாங்கள் பயணத்தை ஒத்திவைத்தோம். maḻai peytatāl nāṅkaḷ payaṇattai ottivaittōm. Because it rained, we put off the trip."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ஒத்திவைத்தேன், ottivaittēṉ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What is put off takes -ஐ: பயணத்தை ஒத்திவை (ottivai), to postpone a journey."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ஒத்திவை (ottivai) is built from otti, the joining form of ஒத்து, \"to move aside, make room\" (DEDR 973), and வை, \"to put\": to put a thing aside for later."
            }
          ]
